WEBVTT

00:03:29.247 --> 00:03:30.581
so they feel closer.

00:03:31.082 --> 00:03:33.834
You really laughed hard
at that "pet frog" line.

00:03:33.834 --> 00:03:35.670
I already feel close to you.

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:36.837
Don’t we feel close?

00:03:36.879 --> 00:03:38.172
JA: Yeah, we feel close.

00:03:38.214 --> 00:03:39.590
NB: There's a lot there.

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:41.842
NB: OK, so what's happening
is when we laugh,

00:03:41.842 --> 00:03:44.720
our brains release a cocktail of hormones.

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:46.514
So we release endorphins,

00:03:46.555 --> 00:03:48.933
giving us a similar feeling
to a runner’s high;

00:03:48.933 --> 00:03:52.019
we lower our cortisol,
making us feel calmer;

00:03:52.019 --> 00:03:55.314
and we release dopamine,
the same hormone released during sex,

00:03:55.314 --> 00:03:57.149
making us feel more bonded.

00:03:57.191 --> 00:03:58.442
So in essence,

00:03:58.484 --> 00:04:00.319
as far as our brains are concerned,